   "etymology": "Uncertain. Attributed to Latin vīvere (“to live”) by Orel, with regular effacement of Latin v /w/ after vowels other than /u/ (cf. latyrë < lavātūra, shqa < sclavus, noshtër < novaster, etc.), although long Latin long i never yields Albanian u in borrowings. Alternatively from Proto-Indo-European *wenh₁- (“to love”) via an intermediate meaning 'to desire, long for'.",
